<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mirza Kuchik Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1880–1921</span> · Also known as Kuchik Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mirza Kuchik Khan was an Iranian revolutionary who from 1915 led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jangal-movement">Jangali movement</a> in the forests of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilan">Gilan</a> against foreign intervention and the weak <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> government. In 1920 he allied with the Bolsheviks to found the Persian Socialist Soviet Republic. After the alliance broke down he fled government forces into the mountains, where he died in 1921.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mirza-kuchik-khan.jpg" alt="Mirza Kuchik Khan" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mirza_Kochak_Khan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
